---
import SimLayout from '../../../layouts/SimLayout.astro';
---

<SimLayout
  areaSlug="machine-learning"
  title="The Curse of Dimensionality"
  description="Space stops behaving as soon as you add axes. Data spreads out until every point is alone, a ball abandons its middle for a paper-thin crust, every distance becomes the same distance, and any two directions you pick are almost certainly at right angles. Five different curses, one slider."
>
  <div class="sim">
    <div class="sim-stage">
      <canvas id="cod" width="900" height="462"></canvas>
    </div>

    <div class="sim-panel">
      <div class="control">
        <label>Which curse</label>
        <div class="seg vert" id="mode">
          <button data-m="sparsity" class="active">Empty space</button>
          <button data-m="shell">Volume in the crust</button>
          <button data-m="distance">All distances equal</button>
          <button data-m="angles">Everything orthogonal</button>
          <button data-m="corners">Nothing but corners</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Dimensions d <b id="dval">2</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="d" min="1" max="120" value="2" />
      </div>

      <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap">
        <button class="btn" id="run">Sweep d</button>
        <button class="btn ghost" id="step">+1</button>
        <button class="btn ghost" id="reset">Reset</button>
      </div>

      <div class="control" data-for="sparsity">
        <label>Fraction of data to capture <b id="fracval">10%</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="frac" min="1" max="50" value="10" />
      </div>

      <div class="control" data-for="shell">
        <label>Crust thickness <b id="epsval">5%</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="eps" min="1" max="40" value="5" />
      </div>

      <div class="control" data-for="sparsity shell distance angles">
        <label>Sample points n <b id="nval">600</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="n" min="100" max="1200" step="50" value="600" />
      </div>

      <div class="readout" id="readout"></div>

      <p class="note" id="note"></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="observe">
    <li>
      <b>Empty space.</b> Cut every axis into 10 bins and the number of cells is
      10<sup>d</sup>. At d = 20 that is a hundred billion billion boxes, and your
      600 points sit in 600 of them. The 2D picture still looks nicely filled,
      which is the trap: <b>every low-dimensional projection lies</b> about how
      crowded the real space is.
    </li>
    <li>
      Watch the curve on the right. To gather 10% of the data you must span
      <b>63% of every axis at d = 5</b> and <b>89% at d = 20</b>. A "local"
      neighbourhood stops being local, so anything built on neighbours (k-NN,
      kernels, histograms) quietly stops being local too.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Volume in the crust.</b> Drag d up and watch the dots evacuate the middle
      of the ball. The outer 5% shell holds under 10% of a 2D disc but over
      <b>99% of a 100D ball</b>. Nothing moved: it is just that volume scales like
      r<sup>d</sup>, so almost all of it is near the surface.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>All distances equal.</b> The cloud around the query point collapses into a
      thin ring: by d = 60 the spread of the distances is only a few percent of
      their mean, and it keeps shrinking like 1/√d. Nearest and farthest stop
      being meaningfully different, which is why exact nearest-neighbour search
      loses its grip in high dimensions.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Everything orthogonal.</b> Two random directions have cos θ with mean 0
      and standard deviation <b>1/√d</b>. By d = 100 nearly every pair sits within
      a few degrees of 90°. High-dimensional space is roomy enough for enormous
      numbers of almost-orthogonal directions, which is exactly what makes random
      projections and superposition in embeddings work.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Nothing but corners.</b> The ball inscribed in a cube touches all 2d faces
      yet fills <b>1 part in 10<sup>28</sup> of it at d = 50</b>. All the volume
      hides in the 2<sup>d</sup> corners, and the cube's half-diagonal is √d while
      its inradius stays 1: the box is really a spiky sea urchin, not a box.
    </li>
  </Fragment>
</SimLayout>

<script>
  import { setupCanvas, makeText } from '../../../lib/sim';

  const canvas = document.getElementById('cod') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  const { ctx, W, H } = setupCanvas(canvas, () => draw());
  const css = (v: string, f = '') =>
    getComputedStyle(canvas).getPropertyValue(v).trim() || f;
  const ink = (a: number) => `rgba(${css('--stage-ink', '232,233,236')},${a})`;
  const { label } = makeText(ctx, ink);

  const AMBER = '#f59e0b';
  const accent = () => css('--accent', '#7c8cff');
  const teal = () => css('--accent-2', '#5eead4');

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Random bank. Every sample is drawn once per seed and stored column-wise, so
  // raising d only appends coordinates to vectors that already exist. The
  // pictures then evolve continuously as the slider moves instead of reshuffling.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  const DMAX = 120;
  const NMAX = 1200;

  function mulberry32(seed: number) {
    let a = seed >>> 0;
    return () => {
      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0;
      let t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a);
      t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;
      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;
    };
  }

  function buildBank(seed: number) {
    const r = mulberry32(seed);
    const gauss = () => {
      const u = Math.max(1e-12, r());
      return Math.sqrt(-2 * Math.log(u)) * Math.cos(2 * Math.PI * r());
    };
    const nrm = new Float32Array(2 * NMAX * DMAX); // vector pairs, for angles
    for (let i = 0; i < nrm.length; i++) nrm[i] = gauss();
    const uni = new Float32Array(NMAX * DMAX); // points in the unit cube
    for (let i = 0; i < uni.length; i++) uni[i] = r();
    const q = new Float32Array(DMAX); // the query point
    for (let i = 0; i < DMAX; i++) q[i] = r();
    const u1 = new Float64Array(NMAX); // one uniform per point, for ball radii
    const ang = new Float64Array(NMAX); // display angle, no maths attached
    for (let i = 0; i < NMAX; i++) {
      u1[i] = r();
      ang[i] = r() * Math.PI * 2;
    }
    return { nrm, uni, q, u1, ang };
  }

  let bank = buildBank(7);

  // --- the five quantities the pictures are built from -----------------------
  const ballRadii = (d: number, n: number) => {
    const out = new Float64Array(n);
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) out[i] = Math.pow(bank.u1[i], 1 / d);
    return out;
  };

  const cosPairs = (d: number, n: number) => {
    const out = new Float64Array(n);
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      let ab = 0,
        aa = 0,
        bb = 0;
      const oa = 2 * i * DMAX,
        ob = (2 * i + 1) * DMAX;
      for (let j = 0; j < d; j++) {
        const a = bank.nrm[oa + j],
          b = bank.nrm[ob + j];
        ab += a * b;
        aa += a * a;
        bb += b * b;
      }
      out[i] = ab / Math.sqrt(aa * bb);
    }
    return out;
  };

  const queryDistances = (d: number, n: number) => {
    const out = new Float64Array(n);
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      let s = 0;
      for (let j = 0; j < d; j++) {
        const t = bank.uni[i * DMAX + j] - bank.q[j];
        s += t * t;
      }
      out[i] = Math.sqrt(s);
    }
    return out;
  };

  /** How many of the 10^d grid cells the n points actually land in. */
  const occupiedCells = (d: number, n: number) => {
    const seen = new Set<string>();
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      let key = '';
      for (let j = 0; j < d; j++)
        key += String.fromCharCode(48 + ((bank.uni[i * DMAX + j] * 10) | 0));
      seen.add(key);
    }
    return seen.size;
  };

  // Volume of the unit ball, in logs: ln V_d = (d/2) ln π − ln Γ(d/2 + 1).
  function lgamma(x: number): number {
    const c = [
      0.99999999999980993, 676.5203681218851, -1259.1392167224028,
      771.32342877765313, -176.61502916214059, 12.507343278686905,
      -0.13857109526572012, 9.9843695780195716e-6, 1.5056327351493116e-7,
    ];
    if (x < 0.5) return Math.log(Math.PI / Math.sin(Math.PI * x)) - lgamma(1 - x);
    x -= 1;
    let a = c[0];
    const t = x + 7.5;
    for (let i = 1; i < 9; i++) a += c[i] / (x + i);
    return 0.5 * Math.log(2 * Math.PI) + (x + 0.5) * Math.log(t) - t + Math.log(a);
  }
  /** log10 of ball volume ÷ enclosing cube volume, for a radius-1 ball. */
  const log10BallOverCube = (d: number) =>
    ((d / 2) * Math.log(Math.PI) - lgamma(d / 2 + 1)) / Math.LN10 -
    d * Math.log10(2);

  // --- state -----------------------------------------------------------------
  const state = {
    mode: 'sparsity',
    d: 2,
    n: 600,
    frac: 10,
    eps: 5,
    playing: false,
  };

  let cache: any = null;
  let cacheKey = '';
  function data() {
    const key = `${state.mode}|${state.d}|${state.n}`;
    if (key === cacheKey && cache) return cache;
    const d = state.d,
      n = state.n;
    let val: any = {};
    if (state.mode === 'sparsity') val = { occ: occupiedCells(d, n) };
    else if (state.mode === 'shell') val = { r: ballRadii(d, n) };
    else if (state.mode === 'distance') val = { dist: queryDistances(d, n) };
    else if (state.mode === 'angles') val = { cos: cosPairs(d, n) };
    cacheKey = key;
    cache = val;
    return val;
  }

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Drawing scaffolding: a square picture on the left, a chart on the right and
  // two caption lines underneath, shared by all five modes.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  const pic = { x: 32, y: 66, w: 344, h: 344 };
  const chart = { x: 468, y: 86, w: 396, h: 288 };
  const dom = { x: [0, 1], y: [0, 1] };
  const mx = (v: number) =>
    chart.x + ((v - dom.x[0]) / (dom.x[1] - dom.x[0])) * chart.w;
  const my = (v: number) =>
    chart.y + chart.h - ((v - dom.y[0]) / (dom.y[1] - dom.y[0])) * chart.h;

  type Tick = { v: number; t: string };
  function chartFrame(
    xd: [number, number],
    yd: [number, number],
    xTicks: Tick[],
    yTicks: Tick[],
    xTitle: string,
    yTitle: string
  ) {
    dom.x = xd;
    dom.y = yd;
    ctx.strokeStyle = ink(0.16);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.strokeRect(chart.x, chart.y, chart.w, chart.h);
    for (const t of yTicks) {
      const y = my(t.v);
      ctx.strokeStyle = ink(0.07);
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(chart.x, y);
      ctx.lineTo(chart.x + chart.w, y);
      ctx.stroke();
      label(t.t, chart.x - 8, y + 4, 0.45, 'right', 10.5);
    }
    for (const t of xTicks) {
      const x = mx(t.v);
      ctx.strokeStyle = ink(0.16);
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(x, chart.y + chart.h);
      ctx.lineTo(x, chart.y + chart.h + 5);
      ctx.stroke();
      label(t.t, x, chart.y + chart.h + 20, 0.45, 'center', 10.5);
    }
    label(yTitle, chart.x, chart.y - 12, 0.42, 'left', 10.5);
    label(xTitle, chart.x + chart.w, chart.y + chart.h + 38, 0.42, 'right', 10.5);
  }

  const dTicks: Tick[] = [
    { v: 1, t: '1' },
    { v: 20, t: '20' },
    { v: 40, t: '40' },
    { v: 60, t: '60' },
    { v: 80, t: '80' },
    { v: 100, t: '100' },
    { v: 120, t: '120' },
  ];

  function curve(f: (x: number) => number, x0: number, x1: number, colour: string) {
    ctx.strokeStyle = colour;
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.beginPath();
    for (let i = 0; i <= 240; i++) {
      const x = x0 + ((x1 - x0) * i) / 240;
      const y = f(x);
      if (i === 0) ctx.moveTo(mx(x), my(y));
      else ctx.lineTo(mx(x), my(y));
    }
    ctx.stroke();
  }

  /** Marks the current d on a curve against dimensions. */
  function dMarker(y: number, text: string) {
    const x = mx(state.d);
    ctx.strokeStyle = ink(0.3);
    ctx.setLineDash([3, 4]);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x, chart.y);
    ctx.lineTo(x, chart.y + chart.h);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);
    ctx.fillStyle = accent();
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(x, my(y), 5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.fill();
    const flip = x > chart.x + chart.w - 90;
    label(
      text,
      flip ? x - 10 : x + 10,
      Math.max(chart.y + 16, my(y) - 12),
      0.95,
      flip ? 'right' : 'left',
      11,
      accent()
    );
  }

  /** Three readable percentage gridlines for a histogram axis. */
  function pctTicks(max: number): Tick[] {
    const step = [0.01, 0.02, 0.05, 0.1, 0.2, 0.5].find((s) => max / s <= 4) ?? 1;
    const out: Tick[] = [];
    for (let v = 0; v <= max + 1e-9; v += step)
      out.push({ v, t: `${Math.round(v * 100)}%` });
    return out;
  }

  function histogram(v: ArrayLike<number>, lo: number, hi: number, bins: number) {
    const counts = new Float64Array(bins);
    let n = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < v.length; i++) {
      const b = Math.floor(((v[i] - lo) / (hi - lo)) * bins);
      if (b >= 0 && b < bins) {
        counts[b]++;
        n++;
      }
    }
    if (n) for (let i = 0; i < bins; i++) counts[i] /= n;
    return counts;
  }

  function drawBars(counts: Float64Array, lo: number, hi: number, colour: string) {
    const bw = (hi - lo) / counts.length;
    ctx.fillStyle = colour;
    for (let i = 0; i < counts.length; i++) {
      if (counts[i] <= 0) continue;
      const x0 = mx(lo + i * bw),
        x1 = mx(lo + (i + 1) * bw);
      const y = my(counts[i]);
      ctx.fillRect(x0 + 0.5, y, Math.max(1, x1 - x0 - 1), chart.y + chart.h - y);
    }
  }

  function vline(x: number, colour: string, text: string, up = 0) {
    const px = mx(x);
    ctx.strokeStyle = colour;
    ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;
    ctx.setLineDash([4, 4]);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, chart.y + 6);
    ctx.lineTo(px, chart.y + chart.h);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);
    if (!text) return;
    const room = chart.x + chart.w - px;
    label(
      text,
      room < 90 ? px - 8 : px,
      chart.y + 18 + up,
      0.95,
      room < 90 ? 'right' : 'center',
      10.5,
      colour
    );
  }

  const picCentre = () => ({
    x: pic.x + pic.w / 2,
    y: pic.y + pic.h / 2,
    R: pic.w * 0.45,
  });

  function picCaption(text: string) {
    label(text, pic.x, pic.y + pic.h + 24, 0.42, 'left', 10.5);
  }

  // --- number formatting -----------------------------------------------------
  function fromLog10(l: number) {
    if (!isFinite(l)) return '—';
    if (l >= -3 && l < 6) {
      const v = Math.pow(10, l);
      return v >= 1000
        ? Math.round(v).toLocaleString()
        : String(+v.toPrecision(3));
    }
    const p = Math.floor(l);
    const m = Math.pow(10, l - p);
    return `${m.toFixed(1)}×10^${p}`;
  }
  const pct = (x: number, dp = 1) => `${(100 * x).toFixed(dp)}%`;
  const sup = (s: string) => s.replace(/\^(-?\d+)/g, '<sup>$1</sup>');

  const readoutEl = document.getElementById('readout') as HTMLElement;
  const noteEl = document.getElementById('note') as HTMLElement;
  function setPanel(rows: [string, string][], note: string) {
    readoutEl.innerHTML = rows
      .map(([k, v]) => `<div class="row"><span>${k}</span><b>${sup(v)}</b></div>`)
      .join('');
    noteEl.innerHTML = note;
  }

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Mode 1: empty space
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  function drawSparsity() {
    const d = state.d,
      n = state.n,
      f = state.frac / 100;
    const { occ } = data();
    const cell = pic.w / 10;

    // which of the 100 visible cells the projected points fall into
    const hit = new Set<number>();
    const pts: [number, number][] = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      const x = bank.uni[i * DMAX];
      const y = d >= 2 ? bank.uni[i * DMAX + 1] : 0.5;
      pts.push([x, y]);
      hit.add(Math.min(9, (x * 10) | 0) * 10 + Math.min(9, (y * 10) | 0));
    }

    ctx.fillStyle = `${accent()}22`;
    for (const k of hit) {
      const cx = Math.floor(k / 10),
        cy = k % 10;
      ctx.fillRect(pic.x + cx * cell, pic.y + pic.h - (cy + 1) * cell, cell, cell);
    }
    ctx.strokeStyle = ink(0.14);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    for (let i = 0; i <= 10; i++) {
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(pic.x + i * cell, pic.y);
      ctx.lineTo(pic.x + i * cell, pic.y + pic.h);
      ctx.moveTo(pic.x, pic.y + i * cell);
      ctx.lineTo(pic.x + pic.w, pic.y + i * cell);
      ctx.stroke();
    }
    ctx.fillStyle = teal();
    for (const [x, y] of pts) {
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(pic.x + x * pic.w, pic.y + pic.h - y * pic.h, 1.7, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
    }

    label(
      `${n} POINTS SEEN THROUGH THEIR FIRST TWO AXES`,
      pic.x,
      pic.y - 16,
      0.5,
      'left',
      11
    );
    picCaption(
      `${hit.size} of these 100 cells are hit · in d = ${d} it is ${occ} of ${fromLog10(d)}`
    );

    chartFrame(
      [1, DMAX],
      [0, 1.05],
      dTicks,
      [
        { v: 0, t: '0' },
        { v: 0.25, t: '25%' },
        { v: 0.5, t: '50%' },
        { v: 0.75, t: '75%' },
        { v: 1, t: '100%' },
      ],
      'dimensions d',
      `SIDE OF THE BOX THAT HOLDS ${state.frac}% OF THE DATA`
    );
    ctx.strokeStyle = ink(0.25);
    ctx.setLineDash([4, 4]);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(mx(1), my(1));
    ctx.lineTo(mx(DMAX), my(1));
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);
    label('the whole axis', mx(DMAX) - 8, my(1) - 8, 0.4, 'right', 10.5);

    const edge = (dd: number) => Math.pow(f, 1 / dd);
    curve(edge, 1, DMAX, teal());
    dMarker(edge(d), `${pct(edge(d), 0)} of each axis`);

    setPanel(
      [
        ['Cells, 10 per axis', fromLog10(d)],
        ['Cells with data in them', String(occ)],
        ['Share of cells occupied', `1 in ${fromLog10(d - Math.log10(occ))}`],
        [`Axis span for ${state.frac}%`, pct(edge(d), 1)],
        ['Points to match d = 1 density', fromLog10(d * Math.log10(n))],
      ],
      `A neighbourhood holding ${state.frac}% of the data needs
       <b>${pct(edge(d), 0)}</b> of every axis at d = ${d}. Past a handful of
       dimensions, "nearby" means "most of the dataset".`
    );
  }

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Mode 2: volume in the crust
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  function drawShell() {
    const d = state.d,
      n = state.n,
      eps = state.eps / 100;
    const { r } = data();
    const c = picCentre();

    ctx.fillStyle = `${AMBER}1f`;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(c.x, c.y, c.R, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.arc(c.x, c.y, c.R * (1 - eps), 0, Math.PI * 2, true);
    ctx.fill();
    ctx.strokeStyle = ink(0.4);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(c.x, c.y, c.R, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.strokeStyle = `${AMBER}99`;
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.setLineDash([3, 4]);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(c.x, c.y, c.R * (1 - eps), 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);

    ctx.fillStyle = teal();
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      const rad = r[i] * c.R;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(
        c.x + rad * Math.cos(bank.ang[i]),
        c.y + rad * Math.sin(bank.ang[i]),
        1.7,
        0,
        Math.PI * 2
      );
      ctx.fill();
    }

    label('UNIFORM POINTS INSIDE THE BALL', pic.x, pic.y - 16, 0.5, 'left', 11);
    label(`outer ${state.eps}%`, c.x, c.y - c.R - 10, 0.75, 'center', 10.5, AMBER);
    picCaption(
      'each dot sits at its true distance from the centre, at an arbitrary angle'
    );

    const bins = 40;
    const counts = histogram(r, 0, 1, bins);
    let maxc = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < bins; i++) maxc = Math.max(maxc, counts[i]);
    const top = Math.max(0.06, maxc * 1.2);
    chartFrame(
      [0, 1],
      [0, top],
      [
        { v: 0, t: '0' },
        { v: 0.25, t: '0.25' },
        { v: 0.5, t: '0.5' },
        { v: 0.75, t: '0.75' },
        { v: 1, t: '1' },
      ],
      pctTicks(top),
      'distance from the centre, r',
      'SHARE OF THE POINTS'
    );
    drawBars(counts, 0, 1, `${teal()}66`);
    // exact bin probabilities: P(r ∈ [a,b]) = b^d − a^d
    ctx.strokeStyle = teal();
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.beginPath();
    for (let i = 0; i < bins; i++) {
      const a = i / bins,
        b = (i + 1) / bins;
      const p = Math.pow(b, d) - Math.pow(a, d);
      const x = mx((a + b) / 2);
      if (i === 0) ctx.moveTo(x, my(p));
      else ctx.lineTo(x, my(p));
    }
    ctx.stroke();
    vline(Math.pow(0.5, 1 / d), accent(), 'half the volume is past here');

    const inCrust = 1 - Math.pow(1 - eps, d);
    setPanel(
      [
        [`Volume in the outer ${state.eps}%`, pct(inCrust, 2)],
        ['Radius splitting it in half', Math.pow(0.5, 1 / d).toFixed(4)],
        ['Mean distance to the centre', (d / (d + 1)).toFixed(4)],
        ['Volume inside half the radius', `1 in ${fromLog10(d * Math.log10(2))}`],
      ],
      `Volume grows like r<sup>d</sup>, so a shell of the last
       <b>${state.eps}%</b> of the radius carries <b>${pct(inCrust, 1)}</b> of the
       ball at d = ${d}. The interior is essentially empty.`
    );
  }

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Mode 3: all distances equal
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  function drawDistance() {
    const d = state.d,
      n = state.n;
    const { dist } = data();
    const c = picCentre();
    const scale = Math.sqrt(d); // the longest distance possible in the cube
    let lo = Infinity,
      hi = 0,
      sum = 0,
      sum2 = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      const u = dist[i] / scale;
      lo = Math.min(lo, u);
      hi = Math.max(hi, u);
      sum += u;
      sum2 += u * u;
    }
    const mean = sum / n;
    const sd = Math.sqrt(Math.max(0, sum2 / n - mean * mean));

    ctx.strokeStyle = ink(0.14);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    for (const f of [0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1]) {
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(c.x, c.y, c.R * f, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.stroke();
    }
    ctx.fillStyle = teal();
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      const rad = (dist[i] / scale) * c.R;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(
        c.x + rad * Math.cos(bank.ang[i]),
        c.y + rad * Math.sin(bank.ang[i]),
        1.7,
        0,
        Math.PI * 2
      );
      ctx.fill();
    }
    for (const [v, col] of [
      [lo, accent()],
      [hi, AMBER],
    ] as [number, string][]) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = col;
      ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(c.x, c.y, v * c.R, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.stroke();
    }
    ctx.fillStyle = accent();
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(c.x, c.y, 5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.fill();

    label('DISTANCE FROM ONE QUERY POINT', pic.x, pic.y - 16, 0.5, 'left', 11);
    label('nearest', c.x, c.y + lo * c.R + 16, 0.9, 'center', 10.5, accent());
    label('farthest', c.x, c.y - hi * c.R - 8, 0.9, 'center', 10.5, AMBER);
    picCaption('every dot at its true distance, angle chosen at random');

    const bins = 44;
    const counts = histogram(
      Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => dist[i] / scale),
      0,
      1,
      bins
    );
    let maxc = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < bins; i++) maxc = Math.max(maxc, counts[i]);
    const top = Math.max(0.06, maxc * 1.25);
    chartFrame(
      [0, 1],
      [0, top],
      [
        { v: 0, t: '0' },
        { v: 0.25, t: '0.25' },
        { v: 0.5, t: '0.5' },
        { v: 0.75, t: '0.75' },
        { v: 1, t: '1' },
      ],
      pctTicks(top),
      'distance ÷ √d',
      'SHARE OF THE POINTS'
    );
    drawBars(counts, 0, 1, `${teal()}77`);
    vline(lo, accent(), '');
    vline(hi, AMBER, '');

    const contrast = (hi - lo) / lo;
    setPanel(
      [
        ['Nearest neighbour', (lo * scale).toFixed(3)],
        ['Farthest point', (hi * scale).toFixed(3)],
        ['(far − near) ÷ near', pct(contrast, 1)],
        ['Spread ÷ mean', pct(sd / mean, 2)],
      ],
      `The farthest of ${n} points is only <b>${pct(contrast, 0)}</b> further away
       than the nearest at d = ${d}. Distances still exist, but they stop
       <b>ranking</b> anything.`
    );
  }

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Mode 4: everything orthogonal
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  function drawAngles() {
    const d = state.d,
      n = state.n;
    const { cos } = data();
    const c = picCentre();

    ctx.strokeStyle = ink(0.16);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(c.x, c.y, c.R, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.strokeStyle = ink(0.2);
    ctx.setLineDash([4, 5]);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(c.x, c.y - c.R);
    ctx.lineTo(c.x, c.y + c.R);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);

    const shown = Math.min(n, 160);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    for (let i = 0; i < shown; i++) {
      const th = Math.acos(Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, cos[i])));
      const s = bank.ang[i] > Math.PI ? 1 : -1;
      ctx.strokeStyle = `${teal()}66`;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(c.x, c.y);
      ctx.lineTo(c.x + c.R * Math.cos(th), c.y + s * c.R * Math.sin(th));
      ctx.stroke();
    }
    ctx.strokeStyle = accent();
    ctx.lineWidth = 3;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(c.x, c.y);
    ctx.lineTo(c.x + c.R, c.y);
    ctx.stroke();

    label('ANGLE TO ONE FIXED DIRECTION', pic.x, pic.y - 16, 0.5, 'left', 11);
    label('reference', c.x + c.R, c.y - 10, 0.9, 'right', 10.5, accent());
    label('90°', c.x + 14, c.y - c.R - 8, 0.45, 'left', 10.5);
    picCaption('160 random directions, each drawn at its true angle');

    const bins = 36;
    const theta = Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => (Math.acos(cos[i]) * 180) / Math.PI);
    const counts = histogram(theta, 0, 180, bins);
    let maxc = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < bins; i++) maxc = Math.max(maxc, counts[i]);
    const top = Math.max(0.08, maxc * 1.25);
    chartFrame(
      [0, 180],
      [0, top],
      [
        { v: 0, t: '0°' },
        { v: 45, t: '45°' },
        { v: 90, t: '90°' },
        { v: 135, t: '135°' },
        { v: 180, t: '180°' },
      ],
      pctTicks(top),
      'angle between two random vectors',
      'SHARE OF THE PAIRS'
    );
    drawBars(counts, 0, 180, `${teal()}66`);

    // theoretical density, ∝ sin^(d−2)θ, normalised to per-bin probability.
    // Below d = 3 it is flat or degenerate, so there is nothing to draw.
    if (d >= 3) {
      const G = 360;
      const f = new Float64Array(G + 1);
      let tot = 0;
      for (let i = 0; i <= G; i++) {
        const th = (Math.PI * i) / G;
        f[i] = Math.pow(Math.sin(th), d - 2);
        tot += f[i];
      }
      ctx.strokeStyle = teal();
      ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      ctx.beginPath();
      for (let i = 0; i <= G; i++) {
        const x = (180 * i) / G;
        const y = (f[i] / tot) * (G / bins);
        if (i === 0) ctx.moveTo(mx(x), my(y));
        else ctx.lineTo(mx(x), my(y));
      }
      ctx.stroke();
    }
    vline(90, accent(), 'orthogonal');

    let near = 0,
      absSum = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      absSum += Math.abs(cos[i]);
      if (theta[i] > 80 && theta[i] < 100) near++;
    }
    const sdDeg = (180 / Math.PI) * (1 / Math.sqrt(d));
    setPanel(
      [
        ['Mean cos θ', '0 exactly'],
        ['Spread of cos θ', `±${(1 / Math.sqrt(d)).toFixed(3)}`],
        ['Mean |cos θ|', (absSum / n).toFixed(3)],
        ['Typical angle', `90° ± ${sdDeg.toFixed(1)}°`],
        ['Pairs within 80°–100°', pct(near / n, 1)],
      ],
      `cos θ has mean 0 and standard deviation <b>1/√d</b>, so two random
       directions in ${d} dimensions land <b>${pct(near / n, 0)}</b> of the time
       within 10° of a right angle.`
    );
  }

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Mode 5: nothing but corners
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  function drawCorners() {
    const d = state.d;
    const c = picCentre();
    const R = c.R;

    // the cube minus the ball: everything left over is corner
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.rect(c.x - R, c.y - R, 2 * R, 2 * R);
    ctx.moveTo(c.x + R, c.y);
    ctx.arc(c.x, c.y, R, 0, Math.PI * 2, true);
    ctx.fillStyle = `${AMBER}30`;
    ctx.fill('evenodd');

    ctx.strokeStyle = ink(0.35);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;
    ctx.strokeRect(c.x - R, c.y - R, 2 * R, 2 * R);
    ctx.strokeStyle = teal();
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(c.x, c.y, R, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.stroke();

    // inradius, always 1, against the half-diagonal, which runs off as √d
    ctx.strokeStyle = teal();
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(c.x, c.y);
    ctx.lineTo(c.x + R, c.y);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.strokeStyle = accent();
    ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;
    ctx.setLineDash([5, 4]);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(c.x, c.y);
    ctx.lineTo(c.x + R, c.y - R);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);
    ctx.fillStyle = accent();
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(c.x, c.y, 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.fill();

    label('BALL INSCRIBED IN A CUBE', pic.x, pic.y - 16, 0.5, 'left', 11);
    label('radius 1', c.x + R / 2, c.y + 18, 0.9, 'center', 11, teal());
    label(
      `√d = ${Math.sqrt(d).toFixed(2)}`,
      c.x + R - 6,
      c.y - R - 8,
      0.9,
      'right',
      11,
      accent()
    );
    label('corners', c.x - R + 10, c.y + R - 12, 0.9, 'left', 11, AMBER);
    picCaption('the shaded part of the box lies outside the ball');

    const lo = -95;
    chartFrame(
      [1, DMAX],
      [lo, 2],
      dTicks,
      [
        { v: 0, t: '1' },
        { v: -20, t: '10^-20' },
        { v: -40, t: '10^-40' },
        { v: -60, t: '10^-60' },
        { v: -80, t: '10^-80' },
      ],
      'dimensions d',
      'BALL VOLUME ÷ CUBE VOLUME'
    );
    curve((dd) => Math.max(lo, log10BallOverCube(dd)), 1, DMAX, teal());
    const ratioLog = log10BallOverCube(d);
    dMarker(Math.max(lo, ratioLog), `1 in ${fromLog10(-ratioLog)}`);

    setPanel(
      [
        ['Ball ÷ cube volume', `1 in ${fromLog10(-ratioLog)}`],
        [
          'Cube volume in the corners',
          ratioLog < -6 ? '99.9999…%' : pct(1 - Math.pow(10, ratioLog), 4),
        ],
        ['Number of corners', fromLog10(d * Math.log10(2))],
        ['Half-diagonal ÷ inradius', `${Math.sqrt(d).toFixed(2)} : 1`],
      ],
      `The ball still touches all ${2 * d} faces, yet at d = ${d} it holds
       <b>1 part in ${fromLog10(-ratioLog).replace(/\^(-?\d+)/, '<sup>$1</sup>')}</b>
       of the box. Corners run off to distance √d while the faces stay at 1.`
    );
  }

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  function draw() {
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    const titles: Record<string, string> = {
      sparsity: 'EMPTY SPACE · data thins out faster than you can sample it',
      shell: 'VOLUME IN THE CRUST · the middle of a ball is a rounding error',
      distance: 'ALL DISTANCES EQUAL · near and far stop being different',
      angles: 'EVERYTHING ORTHOGONAL · random directions meet at 90°',
      corners: 'NOTHING BUT CORNERS · a cube is really a spiky urchin',
    };
    label(titles[state.mode], 32, 34, 0.55, 'left', 12);
    label(`d = ${state.d}`, W - 32, 34, 0.95, 'right', 13, accent());

    if (state.mode === 'sparsity') drawSparsity();
    else if (state.mode === 'shell') drawShell();
    else if (state.mode === 'distance') drawDistance();
    else if (state.mode === 'angles') drawAngles();
    else drawCorners();
  }

  // --- controls --------------------------------------------------------------
  const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as HTMLElement;
  const dSlider = $('d') as HTMLInputElement;
  const runBtn = $('run');

  function syncContext() {
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-for]').forEach((el) => {
      el.style.display = el.dataset.for!.split(' ').includes(state.mode)
        ? ''
        : 'none';
    });
  }

  function sync() {
    $('dval').textContent = String(state.d);
    $('nval').textContent = String(state.n);
    $('fracval').textContent = `${state.frac}%`;
    $('epsval').textContent = `${state.eps}%`;
    dSlider.value = String(state.d);
    draw();
  }

  $('mode').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const b = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!b) return;
    document
      .querySelectorAll('#mode button')
      .forEach((x) => x.classList.remove('active'));
    b.classList.add('active');
    state.mode = b.dataset.m!;
    syncContext();
    sync();
  });
  dSlider.addEventListener('input', () => {
    state.d = +dSlider.value;
    sync();
  });
  $('n').addEventListener('input', (e) => {
    state.n = +(e.target as HTMLInputElement).value;
    sync();
  });
  $('frac').addEventListener('input', (e) => {
    state.frac = +(e.target as HTMLInputElement).value;
    sync();
  });
  $('eps').addEventListener('input', (e) => {
    state.eps = +(e.target as HTMLInputElement).value;
    sync();
  });
  $('step').addEventListener('click', () => {
    state.d = state.d >= DMAX ? 1 : state.d + 1;
    sync();
  });
  $('reset').addEventListener('click', () => {
    state.playing = false;
    runBtn.textContent = 'Sweep d';
    state.d = 2;
    bank = buildBank(7);
    cacheKey = '';
    sync();
  });
  runBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    state.playing = !state.playing;
    runBtn.textContent = state.playing ? 'Pause' : 'Sweep d';
    if (state.playing) requestAnimationFrame(tick);
  });

  let acc = 0;
  let last = 0;
  function tick(t: number) {
    if (!state.playing) return;
    const dt = last ? Math.min(0.1, (t - last) / 1000) : 0;
    last = t;
    acc += dt * 26; // dimensions per second
    if (acc >= 1) {
      const step = Math.floor(acc);
      acc -= step;
      state.d = state.d + step > DMAX ? 1 : state.d + step;
      sync();
    }
    requestAnimationFrame(tick);
  }

  syncContext();
  sync();
</script>

<style>
  .seg.vert {
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: stretch;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .seg.vert button {
    text-align: left;
  }
  .note {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .note :global(b) {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
